{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_y3dhz3zgy4ceq7erkbn6un6ofizpw2gmfsbmpdlpsqgobifyepnq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 15 tests pass. The implementation is complete:\n\n**Summary:**\n- Implemented a port of the C `cset` library — a hash set using **double hashing** with the **xxHash64** non-cryptographic hash algorithm.\n- Translated the xxHash64 algorithm including its variants (`XXH64`, `XXH64_h`), avalanche, finalize, and rounds, preserving exact bit-level semantics with `wrapping_*` arithmetic.\n- Implemented `Cset<T>` with:\n  - Open addressing using `pi == 0` for empty, `pi == -1` for tombstone, and `pi > 0` for occupied slots (preserving the C layout).\n  - `add`, `remove`, `contains`, `clear`, `iter`, `intersect`, `union`, `is_disjoint`, `difference`, plus all the getter/setter accessors.\n  - Custom comparators via `set_comparator`, with byte-wise `memcmp`-style fallback by default.\n  - Resize on max load factor, doubling the capacity (matches `cset__resize`).\n  - Iteration via materializing the live elements into a `Vec<T>` (cloned via `ptr::read`, mirroring the C library's by-value semantics).\n- Used `unsafe` only where the C code requires raw byte access (xxHash works on raw memory) and to manage uninitialized buckets and `pi`-based liveness exactly like the C implementation; safe-Rust drop is handled in a custom `Drop` impl.\n- Tests: `15 passed; 0 failed` under `timeout 60 cargo test`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1086,"cache_read_input_tokens":62248,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1086,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a9097314-09f8-467d-8076-a33302b57709","uuid":"bcb47831-4936-4976-98e9-e73ffcdfaa8b"}
